{
    "_comment": "yunovídeo shell. Four destinations, in the order they matter: Player (the deck: the picture and its transport first, then the queue you curate), Lists (continue watching, the queues you saved, loved and most watched), Library (three ways to look at the same videos — folders, series, all — switched by chips inside the view rather than by three routes) and Sources (the authorised folders, which is where the app explains what it does with your disk). The default route is the player. Rendered as a LEFT vertical rail on desktop and a BOTTOM icon-bar on mobile. The toolbar carries the brand, the language menu, the palette, the theme toggle and a 'more' menu (developer, site map, help), all as events the host acts on. It does NOT carry the pickers: adding videos is Sources' job, and one door is better than three. No backend: a pure gobj tree with hash routing.",
    "shell": {
        "remember_section_position": true,
        "breakpoints": "bulma",
        "zones": {
            "top": {
                "host": "toolbar",
                "show_on": "*"
            },
            "left": {
                "host": "menu.primary",
                "show_on": ">=desktop"
            },
            "bottom": {
                "host": "menu.primary",
                "show_on": "<desktop"
            },
            "center": {
                "host": "stage.main"
            }
        },
        "stages": {
            "main": {
                "zone": "center",
                "default_route": "/player"
            }
        }
    },
